# Contributor Rules (Cursor)

Full rules are in AGENTS.md. This file is the Cursor-specific summary.

## Before making any change

- Read AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md for the authoritative contributor rules.
- Run the verification trio:
  ```
  python -m unittest discover -s tests -t . -v
  python scripts/validate_repository.py
  python scripts/generate_skill_manifests.py --check
  ```

## Architecture rules

- One boundary per skill. Do not duplicate policy, checklists, or review workflow across skills.
- A new skill must pass 4 of 5: (1) distinct trust boundary, (2) different threat model,
  (3) no existing skill that owns it, (4) full 11-file set feasible, (5) real, common failure mode.
- `skill.yaml` files are GENERATED. Change `catalog/skills.json` and run
  `python scripts/generate_skill_manifests.py`.

## What to update when adding or changing a skill

- New skill => `catalog/skills.json` + `AI_INSTRUCTIONS.md` registry row + routing row
  + `README.md` count + `skills/shared/references/skill-graph.md`
  + `skills/shared/references/standards-matrix.md` + `CHANGELOG.md`
- Any change => `CHANGELOG.md` entry under ## [Unreleased]
- Standard re-verified => update version and check-date in the reference file AND in README.md

## Never commit

- `huong dan.md`, `.authoring/`, temp files, scratch files.
- `git add -A` or `git add .` -- stage named paths only.
- Non-ASCII characters outside Vietnamese trigger keywords (use => not ->, straight quotes only).
